From 7642b04310ca30f7444cf072ebfe80c4e4ee5fd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:39:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] microblaze: use the generic __moddi3, drop moddi3.S

MicroBlaze's divide unit is optional, and no multilib in
gcc/config/microblaze/t-microblaze passes -mno-xl-soft-div.  Without it,
libgcc2.c's double-word division and remainder do long division by
32-bit digits, which calls the software __udivsi3, __umodsi3 and
__mulsi3.  __moddi3 comes from config/microblaze/moddi3.S instead, a
shift and subtract loop, and it does so even in a libgcc built with
-mno-xl-soft-div, where it cannot use the divider.

Define TARGET_HAS_NO_HW_DIVIDE and LIBGCC2_MOD_WITHOUT_QUOTIENT unless
__HAVE_HW_DIV__, so that without a divider all four routines divide by
shift and subtract, __moddi3 and __umoddi3 use the remainder-only loop,
and __moddi3 comes from libgcc2.c.  With -mno-xl-soft-div the C uses the
divider.

Mean instructions per call over 4701 operand pairs, under QEMU with
-icount, big-endian; little-endian is within 1%.  "Before" for __moddi3
is moddi3.S in every column:

	              no options       barrel shifter     every option,
	                               and hw multiply    with the divider
	              before   after   before   after     before   after
	__moddi3       522.5   457.0    522.5   275.3      522.5    91.7
	__umoddi3      921.1   338.0    625.6   197.2       54.3    54.3
	__divdi3      1303.3  1312.7    903.7   338.4       88.4    88.4
	__udivdi3      891.1   951.0    626.7   245.4       44.2    44.2

With no options __divdi3 is 0.7% and __udivdi3 6.7% slower on average,
and the worst case rises from 3072 to 5302 and from 3064 to 5376
instructions: shift and subtract costs more than long division when the
quotient is long, and less when it is short.  Long division calls the
software __udivsi3, whose loop branches heavily, so in cycles the
balance may differ; I have not measured cycles on hardware.

moddi3.S rewritten to align the divisor as libgcc2.c does, with no stack
frame, runs at 220.0 instructions per call, faster than the generic
code without a divider.  This patch prefers one generic routine that
can use the divider when there is one.

Tested with gcc.c-torture/execute.exp on qemu-system-microblaze,
machine petalogix-s3adsp1800, against gcc master df809a029: 24536
passes, 14 failures, none of them in division (fprintf-2.c needs a
filesystem; pr117432.c is a separate variadic-argument bug).
arith-rand-ll.c, pr50865.c, pr33669.c and vector-div-neg-pow2.c, which
fail with a broken __moddi3, pass at every optimization level.

[DRAFT: the table and test results are from the previous version of
this series, and are being re-measured.]

libgcc/
	* config/microblaze/microblaze-lib.h: New file.
	* config.host (microblaze*-linux*, microblaze*-*-elf)
	(microblaze*-*-rtems*): Add it to tm_file.
	* config/microblaze/t-microblaze (LIB2FUNCS_EXCLUDE): Remove
	_moddi3.
	(LIB2ADD): Remove moddi3.S.
	* config/microblaze/moddi3.S: Remove.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libgcc/config.host                        |   3 +
 libgcc/config/microblaze/microblaze-lib.h |  37 +++++
 libgcc/config/microblaze/moddi3.S         | 190 ----------------------
 libgcc/config/microblaze/t-microblaze     |   3 +-
 4 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 192 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libgcc/config/microblaze/microblaze-lib.h
 delete mode 100644 libgcc/config/microblaze/moddi3.S

diff --git a/libgcc/config.host b/libgcc/config.host
index 319d6cfe0..81d722968 100644
--- a/libgcc/config.host
+++ b/libgcc/config.host
@@ -1050,14 +1050,17 @@ mcore-*-elf)
 	;;
 microblaze*-linux*)
 	tmake_file="${tmake_file} microblaze/t-microblaze t-fdpbit t-slibgcc-libgcc"
+	tm_file="$tm_file microblaze/microblaze-lib.h"
 	md_unwind_header=microblaze/linux-unwind.h
 	;;
 microblaze*-*-elf)
 	tmake_file="${tmake_file} microblaze/t-microblaze t-fdpbit"
+	tm_file="$tm_file microblaze/microblaze-lib.h"
 	extra_parts="$extra_parts crtbeginS.o crtendS.o crtbeginT.o crti.o crtn.o"
 	;;
 microblaze*-*-rtems*)
 	tmake_file="${tmake_file} microblaze/t-microblaze t-fdpbit"
+	tm_file="$tm_file microblaze/microblaze-lib.h"
 	extra_parts="$extra_parts crtbeginS.o crtendS.o crtbeginT.o crti.o crtn.o"
 	;;
 mips*-*-netbsd*)			# NetBSD/mips, either endian.
diff --git a/libgcc/config/microblaze/microblaze-lib.h b/libgcc/config/microblaze/microblaze-lib.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..75cb367ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libgcc/config/microblaze/microblaze-lib.h
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
